WEBVTT

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:15.150
Skate-leading.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.980
Expressions on ice performed by five skaters.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:24.150
The stage prepared for Ionodai, appearing
in their second Grand Prix finals in a row,

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:30.400
and also the place for the revenge
of the brilliant me, Hayato Sasugai.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.230
Even if I don't have any
trouble with my daily life,

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.150
it's impossible for me to return to competing.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.520
I can't beat my older brother,
Reo Shinozaki, alone,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.560
but it's possible with a team.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.060
It is finally time for the
last program of my challenge.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:52.060
Now, it's time for the Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series finals!

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.400
The Grand Prix finals are already at the climax,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.400
with the short program over

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.900
and the first three teams
starting their free skate.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.400
Where's the competition at now?

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.440
The last team of the first half is skating now.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:07.600
What about Adachi's team?

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.400
They're skating third in the second half,

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.270
so there's still time before they skate.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.310
I see.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:15.310
But, man, high schoolers these days are amazing.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.900
A clean performance!

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.980
As expected of the twins! Perfect!

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:25.520
The average difference in timing for
the start of each move was 0.08 seconds,

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.730
and the difference in pose position is 0.13.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.150
These are pretty high numbers!

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.400
Now for their final skill!

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:40.520
They did it!

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:41.980
A performance with no mistakes!

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:43.900
Chutei University Kamimaezu!

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.100
That's the Mirroring Twins for you!

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.770
The other team members
also matched them precisely.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:51.900
We can expect to see high scores for this!

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:59.520
You seem really at home even though
it's your first time doing commentary, Kuonji.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.940
Now, for the scores!

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.640
Free Skate

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.640
<i>Aichi | </i>Chutei University Kamimaezu High School

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.560
A total of 136.96!

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.810
Chutei University Kamimaezu has set
a personal best at the Grand Prix finals!

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:10.940
Just as you'd expect.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:15.770
Being able to pull out their best at this
crucial moment is proof of their talent!

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:20.560
They pull far ahead of current first place team,
Eimei Academy, to take the top spot!

