00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.190
Only the three schools
in the second half are left!

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.810
Starting with the favorite, St. Clavis,

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:28.730
with the "Top of Kings,"
Shinozaki, on their team,

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.650
and including Kogahara High and Ionodai,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.850
the second half is full of teams to watch!

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.730
The second half of the
free skate will begin shortly!

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:39.730
Which team will grasp victory in the end?!

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:13.520
Episode 11

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:13.520
Perfect

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.270
Here at Makuhari Ice Arena,

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.690
where the Boys' High School Skate-Leading
Grand Prix Series finals are being held,

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:27.020
there are only three schools left to skate
in the Grand Prix finals free skate.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:31.940
I, Takai, will be doing the play-by-play
with commentary by Noa Kuonji.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:33.270
Thank you for having me.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:34.730
Right now, they are smoothing the ice

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:39.060
to prepare for the performances
of the three teams in the second half.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:43.100
Let's use this time to recap what's
happened in the competition so far.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.060
Okay.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:45.480
In the short program,

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.150
as expected, the ones who ended up at the top

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:50.560
were last year's champions,
the emperors--St. Clavis Gakuin!

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.690
They are exceptionally consistent.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:56.940
Throughout the whole series,
they have never given up the top spot.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:00.650
It no longer seems possible
to imagine this team losing.

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:04.100
Next, in second place was the team
that just finished their free skate,

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.350
Chutei University Kamimaezu High School.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:08.520
As expected, the schools that regularly
make the finals are strong.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:11.270
The specialty of the Mirroring Twins,
the Ishikawa brothers,

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:13.310
also works well in the short program.

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:15.310
They were able to skate to their strengths.

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:19.230
They were followed by Kogahara
High School and Ionodai High School.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:22.730
These are the overall standings after
the first half of the free program.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.150
What do you think of these results, Kuonji?

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:29.730
Naturally, Chutei University High
has received a top score.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:31.650
With this, the winners must
beat either Chutei High

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:34.980
or one of the teams skating in the second half,

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:40.060
but for Kogahara and Ionodai,
this is a very high hurdle to overcome.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:40.900
What do you mean?

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.900
In order for one of these two schools to win,

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.900
they need to beat Chutei High's total score

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:49.900
from the short program and free skate.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:54.350
However, even if you add the
highest scores they got this season,

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.190
they are still just barely under Chutei High.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:01.650
Which means they will also need
to skate their best performances.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:03.770
Yes, and surpass their past selves.

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:08.850
However, there is the expectation
that both schools will do just that.

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:13.020
Of course, we can't rule out
St. Clavis Gakuin, either.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:16.350
So you're saying we're in for a bumpy ride?

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:20.020
The second half of the free skate
performances are about to start.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.980
The 6-minute practice is now over.

