00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.060
We're going last.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:29.650
Don't let your bodies get cold.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:32.480
It's fine, it's fine. We know.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.310
Aki!

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:36.020
Jonouchi, how's your stomach?

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.100
Does it hurt?

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:40.400
I'm fine. I took some
medicine just in case, too.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.480
Don't get too fired up.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.270
I know.

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:53.100
I'm just keeping my energy
at the right level for the performance.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.600
That's fine then.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.350
You guys understand, right?

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.190
Yes, sir!

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:59.650
If we skate like we always do,
we can win. But, that doesn't mean--

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:04.020
We said, we know. We're not
too nervous or too relaxed.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.440
Please trust us.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:07.350
You're right.

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:09.480
Maeshima's watching, huh?

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:21.400
Even so, he can't surpass me.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:25.020
Please make the small adjustments
to the routine as I told you.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.060
Do you remember them?

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:27.270
Yes, sir!

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:30.440
During the time you're about to spend on the ice

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:33.940
no one else can get in the way.
This time belongs only to you.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:35.560
Go out and give it your all!

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:36.810
Yes, sir!

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:39.770
--All right!
--Let's do this!

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.440
Himekawa.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.560
About yesterday.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.100
We were serious about what we said.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.770
Thank you for waiting.

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:52.520
The second half of the
free skate will now begin.

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:57.310
Now, this year's Grand Prix Series

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.940
is finally down to the free skate
of the last three teams.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:02.690
What conclusion is waiting at the end?!

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:06.770
Skating fourth, Niigata Prefectural
Kogahara High School.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:24.980
Kogahara High School is skating with
Himekawa in the single lead position.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.980
It's a standard tactic.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:28.600
The ace racks up the points

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:32.650
while the other members build
a base steadily with basic points.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:34.770
It's a simple strategy,
but it's a good way to get results.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:36.020
But with that...

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:38.770
...it's hard to improve on
their personal best by much...

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:47.730
I set a limit on my own abilities.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.440
But back then...

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.770
...something changed in me.

00:08:51.770 --> 00:08:54.480
I thought I could still go further.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.440
That's why I changed teams.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:09:02.190
So that I could reexamine myself
under the direction of my old coach.

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:06.480
When I joined my current team, I was prepared.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:08.440
I'd abandoned this team before.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:12.350
I didn't think they'd accept me again so easily.

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:15.480
It’s a dream to have
a chance of going to finals.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.100
I’m very grateful.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:20.560
I didn't think they'd say that to me.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:22.450
Shisen-en

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:26.310
Himekawa, skate to your heart's content.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:30.690
Our style is to support you, our ace
and one lead, and make you look good.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:32.730
But you haven't been
skating seriously, have you?

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:34.270
You've been holding back for our sakes.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:36.980
It's pathetic that we made you
feel you needed to, though.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:38.690
No, it's not...

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:40.980
What did you transfer here to do?

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:44.770
So you could fight against Shinozaki
and Maeshima and the others, right?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.190
Show us our ace winning!

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:49.150
We've been practicing, too!

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.230
We can do it!

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:52.900
Pour out everything you've got, Himekawa!

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:58.400
But if I fail, the everything will collapse.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.310
Himekawa!

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:01.150
Let's do it!

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:03.440
We can keep up with you!

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:04.850
Even if you don't do it...

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:07.270
...we'll do it by ourselves!

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:13.270
What's this?

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:16.020
They've changed their routine to include
consecutive jumps by the whole team!

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:17.400
That's nice!

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.850
As Himekawa's in the air
with his quadruple jump,

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:23.020
his teammates match him with triples!

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:25.440
This is really difficult!

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:26.980
Remember what the coach said?

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:29.440
This time belongs to us!

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:36.650
They did it!

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:38.230
This is wonderful, too!

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:40.350
Their whole performance has gotten sharper!

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:43.100
And they're far better than
they have been until now.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.730
So this is Himekawa's real power...?

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:50.350
Man, he's completely thrown off my calculations.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:51.600
But...

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:54.690
That's only if the other guys
can keep up with him until the end.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:07.350
We can do it...

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:11.020
I can test... my strength at nationals!

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.980
A quadruple Axel! He landed it perfectly!

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:23.980
His teammates are standing firm, too!

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:24.940
We can do it...!

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:27.940
We can do it!

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.350
The winners will be...

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:30.560
...us!

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:34.980
They really did it...

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:47.400
There it is! They did it!

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.190
Kogahara High had no mistakes!

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:50.690
A wonderful performance!

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:53.440
Their ace, Himekawa's performance was amazing,

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:56.150
but his teammates also did their best!

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:59.060
It was "One for all, and all for one!"

00:11:59.060 --> 00:11:59.900
What do you think?

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:03.480
Their improvement from the middle
to the end was amazing.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:05.770
I've never seen Himekawa skate like that...

00:12:05.770 --> 00:12:08.850
And their points. How much
were they able to get with that...?

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:11.150
Damn it, that guy really is cool!

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:13.400
What, a rare compliment from you?

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:16.520
I'm not complimenting him!
I'll send him flying, anyway!

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:19.730
I can only hope it'll be that easy...

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:22.060
Now, it looks like their scores are coming!

