00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.020
{=8}Niigata                                      Kogahara High School

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:40.690
And, they've exceeded
Chutei University High's score,

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:43.020
jumping into the lead!

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:47.100
With this, Ionodai is in an
even more difficult situation.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:52.850
Of course, this isn't an easy score
to beat even for St. Clavis!

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:10.650
Wow, Kogahara High got a huge
score there, huh, Kuonji?

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:13.190
They've increased their personal best by a lot.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:16.810
Seriously. They surpassed my predictions!

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:19.770
With this, St. Clavis can't be careless.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:21.310
To top Kogahara's score,

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:26.020
St. Clavis will have to score higher than
their series average free skate score.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:29.310
In other words, a single miss
could cost them the victory.

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:31.520
Moreover, in this series,

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:34.230
Shinozaki has needed to work
on the entertainment aspect.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:37.270
Compared to the technical score,
his performance score has been low.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:41.520
Of course, we're talking about
an overall high level here, though.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:47.150
But if he doesn't overcome this,
the unlikely could become more likely.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.310
If we stay here, we'll be
in the way of the next team.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:55.440
Come on, let's go.

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:56.480
Yes, sir!

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:58.900
Himekawa.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.100
You really are amazing.

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:04.150
But, too bad.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.480
Well, they got a higher score than expected,

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:18.020
so our path to two consecutive wins
has become less smooth. But--

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:19.730
It doesn't matter.

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:23.400
We'll do it. The way we always do, calmly.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.730
And that's how we'll win.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:26.230
Yeah.

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:29.060
Shinozaki, it'll be the same as before.

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:31.850
In the places where we can leave it up
to the lead's discretion, we'll follow you.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:32.980
Got it?

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:36.900
"The same as always" is the hardest to do, though.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:37.980
But it's just like Taiga.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.150
Yeah...

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:41.650
Are you really okay with that?

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:45.150
If you don't get a ton of points,
then we'll get past you.

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:47.270
It's disgraceful to bluff.

00:14:47.270 --> 00:14:50.480
If you boast too much, you'll look foolish.

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.270
Do you guys also--

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:03.270
It looks like your whole team
feels the same way, huh?

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:08.940
Skating fifth, Tokyo's
St. Clavis Gakuin High School.

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:09.980
Captain.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:11.600
Yeah, it's time.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:12.600
Let's go.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.810
Not shaking even a little, huh?

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:23.900
Like they're full of confidence.

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:27.270
To skate perfectly at that
level is impossible, though.

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:31.690
Even so, to Himuro and his team,
it's like they have to anyway...

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:34.400
Shinozaki didn't even hear any of it.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:36.690
He's already focused on his performance.

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:38.690
That's fine.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:41.650
It wouldn't be interesting otherwise!

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:43.900
Now, they're finally here.

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.600
In all three competitions
they appeared in this year,

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:48.850
they took the top in both
the short program and free skate.

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:51.440
They've been coasting
to a second consecutive win.

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:55.440
But Kogahara High's performance
right before this got a high score.

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:58.730
It's the first time a big obstacle
has appeared before them.

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:02.060
Will they be able to push that aside
to win the laurels a second time?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:05.190
All eyes are on St. Clavis Gakuin!

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:06.940
This feels pretty good.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:10.770
We've got a goal to beat,
and the audience is expecting that.

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:15.690
Even so, don't go crazy like Ionodai's red dog.

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:19.940
Let's go!

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:24.310
Now, what kind of performance
will St. Clavis Gakuin show us?

00:16:30.310 --> 00:16:35.810
The music starts slow, but look at
how sharp everyone's movements are!

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:38.480
There's also Shinozaki's swordsmanship.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:42.270
It looks like they've borrowed
techniques from rhythmic gymnastics.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:45.270
He's even doing jumps while holding his sword.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:49.440
His technique really is impeccable.

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:01.690
This guy really is amazing.

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:08.940
Yamashita and I resisted at first when
Shinozaki and Kurayoshi joined the club.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:13.440
Why? Why make them first string without
even testing them on second string?

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:16.440
And to put Fujiwara and Matsumoto on reserve!

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.150
Are you saying they should be starters?!

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:23.690
You know, right? The second string guys
have been working hard to get here!

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:26.350
They're the coach's instructions.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.440
Can't accept it?

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:30.940
Let us skate a match between them!

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:33.520
It won't be too late
to decide things after that.

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:38.980
In the end, we lost badly...

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:52.230
I don't really understand
what "entertainment" is.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:55.850
That's why I've come here to learn that.

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:57.650
Please take care of me.

00:17:57.650 --> 00:17:59.270
He's been called a genius

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:02.270
and defeated national-level skaters,

00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:04.900
but he's still trying to learn something.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:09.850
From that day on, we changed.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:16.310
We tried to learn Shinozaki's techniques
and make them our own.

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:18.310
It was strange, but when we did that,

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:21.600
the hard practices we had before became fun.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:24.650
We could tell that we were improving every day.

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:27.310
And it made us proud.

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:29.810
That the only ones who could
perform what Shinozaki wanted...

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:31.520
...was us!

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:40.900
This is amazing.

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:42.980
All five of them doing consecutive jumps!

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:46.310
Their timing and the height of
their jumps--everything was perfect!

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:49.100
Above all, to be able
to keep up with Shinozaki--

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.560
The other four are amazingly skilled!

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:56.310
Shinozaki catches it beautifully!

00:18:56.310 --> 00:18:59.980
Just as planned, Yamashita and
Michinaga both improved.

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:01.850
And Shinozaki, too--

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:03.940
He needs work on the entertainment aspect?

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:06.690
No, he's a perfectionist,

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:10.100
so he didn't want to show what he had
until he was satisfied with it himself.

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:13.350
With the high level of technique
and expression cultivated in singles,

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:14.900
and the body he was blessed with,

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:18.060
when you add "entertainment,"

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:21.270
an overwhelming charisma is born!

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:34.650
This feels good...

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:41.730
These high-level skaters
who could meet my demands...

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:44.650
I still cannot see the greatest performance...

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:50.770
But beyond the best performance
I can do with these teammates,

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:55.520
I might be able to see the greatest
performance that I'm after.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:57.690
So...

00:19:57.690 --> 00:20:00.100
...just follow me quietly!

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:09.650
They did it! A combination skill
with all team members!

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:11.520
It's a revelry of moves!

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:13.900
No one watching could take
their eyes off for a second!

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:15.600
We're all mesmerized!

00:20:15.600 --> 00:20:17.900
And now, for their final move...

00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:21.440
This was also completed beautifully!

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:37.940
They did it!

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:43.350
Completing their last skill, St. Clavis Gakuin
finishes their performance!

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:44.730
Just stunning.

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:48.650
If anyone had made a mistake during those
difficult consecutive moves at the end,

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:51.270
it could have thrown off
their whole performance.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:56.060
But they all skated perfectly,
without any mistakes.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:59.440
This is a performance that could
only be done by St. Clavis Gakuin,

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:02.850
where every skater is highly skilled.

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:12.400
Beat <i>them</i> ...?

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:14.150
Are you stupid?

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:17.350
How is anyone supposed to do that...?

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:36.060
Tokyo |

